; Container scene for sm_jeep_turret.gltf -- the Integration-phase artefact.
;
; Inherited from the imported glTF (the root node carries `instance=`), so
; re-exporting the model flows straight through and only what is added here is
; owned by this file. Per PIPELINE.md, material overrides and gameplay attachment
; points belong on this scene; the imported .gltf is never edited.
;
; The Marker3D nodes are attachment points for gameplay code. Positions are in
; Godot space: +X right, +Y up, -Z forward. Markers parented under turret_yaw /
; turret_pitch move with the turret; the rest are fixed to the hull.
;
; mk_steering_axis exists because the steering column is raked ~22 degrees and the
; glTF could not carry that rotation -- gltf_transforms.py fails this asset on any
; node rotation over 0.5 degrees, so every pivot Empty in the model is identity.
; The tilt lives here instead, where nothing validates it. Rotate the wheel with
; steering_wheel_pivot.rotate(mk_steering_axis.global_basis.z, angle) rather than
; about a local cardinal axis.
;
; Note for the prefab layer: the -convcolonly proxies import as StaticBody3D nodes
; under `collision`. A drivable vehicle wants a VehicleBody3D, so reuse the
; generated ConvexPolygonShape3D resources under your own body rather than driving
; these directly.

